                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>During the morning of December 16 Secretary Dulles discussed the Trieste question
                    with Italian Prime Minister Pella for three quarters of an hour. In setting up
                    the meeting Secretary Dulles had told Pella that he was unwilling to go into
                    details on the subject or negotiate about it. The United States Delegation
                    reported the substance of the discussion in telegram 2319 from Paris, December
                    16, which is printed in the compilation on Trieste in volume VIII.</p>
            </div>
